      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T12:50:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. CONFIG_TEGRA_HOST1X_CONTEXT_BUS does not enable the full Host1x driver. It enables a small built-in bus object required by the core IOMMU code. The Host1x driver itself remains a vendor module.\n\nBecause this is a hidden core-kernel option, host1x.ko cannot enable it after GKI is built. GKI already uses similar hidden configuration groups for vendor dependencies, such as GKI_HIDDEN_QCOM_CONFIGS.\n\nFurthermore, the same Tegra configuration was accepted for Android 15/6.6 in change 3634732 (https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3634732).",
      "parentUuid": "9e15a53e_272d5bd4",
